  "summary": "The glossy, nature-tech optimism of 2004-2013 tech design: aqua gloss, skeuomorphs, bubbles, grass and sky-blue gradients.",
  "description": "Named retroactively (2017, Consumer Aesthetics Research Institute) after font designer Adrian Frutiger, Frutiger Aero describes the era of Windows Vista/7 Aero, iOS skeuomorphism, glossy buttons, tropical fish wallpapers, water droplets and sustainability-utopian eco-tech imagery. It promised a clean, humane digital future; skeuomorphism and gloss were killed by flat design (~2013). Revived nostalgically since 2022 as the \"glossy optimism\" counterpoint to flat corporate sameness.",
